All 4 tests pass. The fix is straightforward:

**Bug**: Line 43 used `foodSurplus >= 0`, which treated a zero surplus (production equals consumption) the same as a positive surplus. This caused population to grow even in settlements that were merely breaking even on food.

**Fix**: Changed `>=` to `>`, so population only grows when there is an actual surplus — food produced strictly exceeds food consumed.


